{
  "section": "CRS-06",
  "name": "sealed-sender-v1-decrypt",
  "description": "Sealed sender v1: decryption of a sealed message with the recipient identity private key to the sealed inner message (field inner). The sealed messages (ciphertexts) are oracle outputs made with a random ephemeral key, so the vector is decrypt-only. The fields stage1_*_key, stage2_*_key, sender_identity_public and inner were recomputed by an author-written re-derivation from the CRS-06 text with standard X25519, HKDF, AES-CTR and HMAC, and matched the oracle decryption byte-for-byte. inner_* and sender_* fields are the oracle parse of the sealed inner message and its sender certificate. Certificates chain to the vector trust root; server certificate key id 1. Rejection reasons (fields named reason or error_if_*) are neutral paraphrases of the oracle result, not its text.",
  "pin": "libsignal v0.103.0",
